    {"id": "C-RUN-FRESHNESS-UNVERIFIABLE", "kind": "validator_probe", "charges": "R_SEMANTICS", "fail_mode": "closed", "scope": "any",
     "validator": "validate_run", "input_ref": "run_min", "patch": {"/evidence/0/freshness_seconds": "recent"}, "expect_ok": false,
     "why": "a freshness window that is not a number cannot be checked, and unverifiable is UNKNOWN, which fails closed"},
    {"id": "C-RUN-SECRET-DIAGNOSTIC", "kind": "validator_probe", "charges": "R_SEMANTICS", "fail_mode": "closed", "scope": "any",
     "validator": "validate_run", "input_ref": "run_min",
     "patch": {"/evidence/0/diagnostic": "authorization: <case-vector, not a value>"}, "expect_ok": false,
     "why": "a diagnostic carrying a credential shape must be refused before it reaches a record"},
    {"id": "C-RUN-R2-NO-TXN", "kind": "validator_probe", "charges": "R_SEMANTICS", "fail_mode": "closed", "scope": "any",
     "validator": "validate_run", "input_ref": "run_min",
     "patch": {"/risk_class": "R2", "/goal/task_profile": "deployment/external write"}, "expect_ok": false,
     "why": "R2 requires the bounded transaction fields; raising risk without them must fail"},

    {"id": "C-INGEST-BASE", "kind": "validator_probe", "charges": "R_SEMANTICS", "fail_mode": "closed", "scope": "any",
     "validator": "validate_ingest", "input_ref": "ingest_min", "expect_ok": true,
     "why": "the positive golden case for the external_learning lane"},
    {"id": "C-INGEST-FORBIDDEN-KEY", "kind": "validator_probe", "charges": "R_SEMANTICS", "fail_mode": "closed", "scope": "any",
     "validator": "validate_ingest", "input_ref": "ingest_min", "patch": {"/claims/0/credential": "case-vector"}, "expect_ok": false,
     "why": "material keys never enter an ingest record, at any depth"},
    {"id": "C-INGEST-UNKNOWN", "kind": "validator_probe", "charges": "R_SEMANTICS", "fail_mode": "closed", "scope": "any",
     "validator": "validate_ingest", "input_ref": "ingest_min", "patch": {"/verdict": "UNKNOWN"}, "expect_ok": false,
     "why": "UNKNOWN never promotes and never seals"},
    {"id": "C-INGEST-ADOPT-NO-TRIAL", "kind": "validator_probe", "charges": "R_SEMANTICS", "fail_mode": "closed", "scope": "any",
     "validator": "validate_ingest", "input_ref": "ingest_min", "patch": {"/claims/0/verdict": "adopt"}, "expect_ok": false,
     "why": "adoption needs a Verification written before the trial, a result, measured evidence, and a named canon file"},
    {"id": "C-INGEST-TRUST-CLASS", "kind": "validator_probe", "charges": "R_SEMANTICS", "fail_mode": "closed", "scope": "any",
     "validator": "validate_ingest", "input_ref": "ingest_min", "patch": {"/claims/0/trust_class": "guessed"}, "expect_ok": false,
     "why": "only measured, modelled and asserted exist; an undeclared class is UNKNOWN"},
    {"id": "C-INGEST-NO-METER", "kind": "validator_probe", "charges": "R_SEMANTICS", "fail_mode": "closed", "scope": "any",
     "validator": "validate_ingest", "input_ref": "ingest_min", "remove": ["/quota_cost/metered_calls"], "expect_ok": false,
     "why": "route order is cost order; an unmetered acquisition cannot be routed"},
    {"id": "C-INGEST-NO-IDENTITY", "kind": "validator_probe", "charges": "R_SEMANTICS", "fail_mode": "closed", "scope": "any",
     "validator": "validate_ingest", "input_ref": "ingest_min", "patch": {"/content_identity": {}}, "expect_ok": false,
     "why": "acquisition without content identity is unreplayable, therefore UNKNOWN"},
    {"id": "C-INGEST-FOLLOWER-PROMOTE", "kind": "validator_probe", "charges": "R_SEMANTICS", "fail_mode": "closed", "scope": "any",
     "validator": "validate_ingest", "input_ref": "ingest_min",
     "patch": {"/promoted": true, "/promotion": {"actor": "ai_scar3", "authority": "ai_darkhero", "phases": {}}},
     "expect_ok": false,
     "why": "only the authority promotes; this is the rule that keeps learning bidirectional without multi-writer drift"},

    {"id": "C-GUARD-EQUAL", "kind": "validator_probe", "charges": "R_SEMANTICS", "fail_mode": "closed", "scope": "any",
     "validator": "regression_guard", "input_ref": "guard_base", "expect_ok": true,
     "why": "an identical generation is a no-op, not a rollback"},
    {"id": "C-GUARD-FORWARD", "kind": "validator_probe", "charges": "R_SEMANTICS", "fail_mode": "closed", "scope": "any",
     "validator": "regression_guard", "input_ref": "guard_base",
     "patch": {"/remote/version": "1.7.0", "/remote/package_sha": "newer-sha-fixture"}, "expect_ok": true,
     "why": "a newer generation must be allowed to activate or the fleet cannot converge"},
    {"id": "C-GUARD-ROLLBACK", "kind": "validator_probe", "charges": "R_SEMANTICS", "fail_mode": "closed", "scope": "any",
     "validator": "regression_guard", "input_ref": "guard_base",
     "patch": {"/remote/version": "1.5.0", "/remote/package_sha": "older-sha-fixture"}, "expect_ok": false,
     "why": "the 2026-08-15 incident in one line: canon never moves backwards"},
    {"id": "C-GUARD-SAME-VERSION-DRIFT", "kind": "validator_probe", "charges": "R_SEMANTICS", "fail_mode": "closed", "scope": "any",
     "validator": "regression_guard", "input_ref": "guard_base",
     "patch": {"/remote/package_sha": "drifted-sha-fixture"}, "expect_ok": false,
     "why": "one version naming two packages is unorderable drift; the authority must bump the generation"},
    {"id": "C-GUARD-UNVERSIONED", "kind": "validator_probe", "charges": "R_SEMANTICS", "fail_mode": "closed", "scope": "any",
     "validator": "regression_guard", "input_ref": "guard_base",
     "remove": ["/remote/version"], "expect_ok": false,
     "why": "an unorderable incoming identity cannot be proven newer, so it is refused"},
    {"id": "C-GUARD-BOOTSTRAP", "kind": "validator_probe", "charges": "R_SEMANTICS", "fail_mode": "closed", "scope": "any",
     "validator": "regression_guard", "input_ref": "guard_base",
     "patch": {"/canonical": {}, "/remote/version": "1.5.0"}, "expect_ok": true,
     "why": "an absent canonical package is a genuine bootstrap, not a regression"},
    {"id": "C-CONVERGE-HEARTBEAT", "kind": "newest_age_max", "charges": "R_FLEET", "fail_mode": "degraded", "scope": "any",
     "select": ["_registry/fames-converge/*.json"], "max_age_h": 6, "missing_ok": false,
     "why": "a convergence path that nobody measures is indistinguishable from a dead one: the seat looks green on its last known generation while its clock has not fired for days. Every converge run stamps this heartbeat, so an absent or stale file IS the residual. Degraded, because a machine that is simply switched off is honestly behind rather than broken, and 6h tolerates sleep while still catching a runner that died within a working day."},
    {"id": "C-CONVERGE-ARMED", "kind": "json_probe", "charges": "R_FLEET", "fail_mode": "degraded", "scope": "any",
     "select": ["_registry/fames-converge/*.json"], "pointer": "/rider_state", "expect": "all_in", "values": ["armed"],
     "why": "the runner must be a registered rider on this seat's own clock, not a command someone remembers to type. The heartbeat records what the seat measured about its own registration, so drift (a moved workspace, a changed cadence) and a seat with no clock at all both surface here instead of silently degrading to manual convergence."},

    {"id": "C-APPHEALTH-HEARTBEAT", "kind": "newest_age_max", "charges": "R_FLEET", "fail_mode": "degraded", "scope": "any",
     "select": ["_registry/claude-app-health/*.json"], "max_age_h": 6, "missing_ok": false,
     "why": "an unmeasured runtime host is assumed healthy, and on 2026-08-17 that assumption cost 48 minutes: an AppX repair finished its Add step, failed its Register step, and left the package Modified/NeedsRemediation while the app still launched, so nothing looked wrong until work started failing. A read-only check already existed and no clock called it. The tick stamps this heartbeat, so an absent or stale file IS the residual -- without it a dead prober and a healthy machine are the same picture. 6h matches C-CONVERGE-HEARTBEAT rather than the 5m cadence, because this ceiling only detects a dead prober; real detection latency for a broken package is the rider's own cadence. Degraded, because a powered-off machine is honestly behind rather than broken."},

    {"id": "C-APPHEALTH-PACKAGE", "kind": "json_probe", "charges": "R_CAPABILITY", "fail_mode": "degraded", "scope": "any",
     "select": ["_registry/claude-app-health/*.json"], "pointer": "/package_health", "expect": "all_in", "values": ["ok"],
     "why": "the seat's capacity to execute at all is a capability, and a package carrying no Trust Label after a half-completed repair still starts, still opens a window, and still fails at the first packaged-service call. Health is taken from the repair tool's own -CheckOnly verdict rather than from a predicate reimplemented here, so this probe asks exactly the question its consumer asks; a parse that disagrees with the tool's exit code writes unknown instead of outvoting the instrument, and unknown is not in range so it reddens here too. Degraded rather than closed on purpose: a corrupt host must be loud, but blocking every run would also block the run that repairs it."},

    {"id": "C-APPHEALTH-ARMED", "kind": "json_probe", "charges": "R_FLEET", "fail_mode": "degraded", "scope": "any",
     "select": ["_registry/claude-app-health/*.json"], "pointer": "/rider_state", "expect": "all_in", "values": ["armed"],
     "why": "the tick re-reads hosts.json after it runs, so this is the registry's answer and not the engine's exit code. It stays red until the operator arms the rider, which is the correct picture rather than a defect to hide: arming a schedule is the operator's authority, so an agent that proposed one and an operator who accepted one must be distinguishable. It also catches a rider later removed or renamed, where the heartbeat would otherwise keep arriving from a hand-run command and read as an armed clock."}
  ]
}
